node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log

# Compiler output emitted BESIDE its source, which happens when tsc is run
# without -outDir. Two reasons this must never be committed or left lying
# around: on a public repo it is 44 files of noise, and — more seriously — this
# codebase uses ESM with explicit `.js` extensions on relative imports
# (`import './amount.js'`), so a stale `amount.js` next to `amount.ts` can win
# at runtime resolution and quietly test code that no longer exists.
# The real build output goes to packages/*/dist, already ignored above.
packages/*/src/**/*.js
packages/*/src/**/*.d.ts
packages/*/src/**/*.js.map
packages/*/src/**/*.d.ts.map
scripts/**/*.js
scripts/**/*.d.ts
scripts/**/*.js.map
scripts/**/*.d.ts.map
# Configuration lives in docker-compose.yml now and `.env.example` is gone, but these stay: docker
# compose still reads a `.env` beside the compose file (HOST_PORT is the one thing left that comes
# from it), people make one out of habit, and the day one of them puts a real secret in it is the
# day this line is the only thing standing between that secret and a public repository.
.env
.env.local
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-*
data/snapshots/
e2e/.tmp/
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
